<section class="usecases" id="usecases" aria-labelledby="usecases-title">
<div class="uc-top">
<h2 id="usecases-title">Use cases for the sites you run</h2>
<p class="uc-lead">One connected system for facilities, assets, and the teams on site.</p>
</div>
<div class="uc-fan">
<a class="uc-card" href="/stories/asset-management" aria-label="Assets. 50,000+ assets traced. A full audit now takes 30 minutes.">
<span class="uc-face">
<span class="uc-pill">Assets</span>
<strong>50,000+ assets traced. A full audit now takes <b>30 minutes</b>.</strong>
<span class="uc-copy">The register lived in finance. RFID tags now tie every asset to its place, purchase order, and invoice.</span>
<span class="uc-stats">
<span><b>30 min</b> for a full audit, down from 15 working days</span>
<span><b>60%</b> lower warehouse rental from the first month</span>
<span><b>4,120</b> ghost assets removed from the books</span>
<span><b>100%</b> of assets mapped to one purchase order and invoice</span>
</span>
</span>
</a>
<a class="uc-card" href="/stories/facility-operations" aria-label="Campuses. 14 sites. One way of working.">
<span class="uc-face">
<span class="uc-pill">Campuses</span>
<strong><b>14 sites</b>. One way of working, in six cities.</strong>
<span class="uc-copy">Every campus had its own routine. One set of SOPs, checklists, and asset records now runs them all.</span>
<span class="uc-stats">
<span><b>14</b> campuses on one standard way of working</span>
<span><b>32,000+</b> assets tracked, with service history</span>
<span><b>5 days</b> to open a new campus, down from 3 weeks</span>
<span><b>45%</b> fewer unplanned breakdowns</span>
</span>
</span>
</a>
<a class="uc-card" href="/stories/pantry" aria-label="Pantry. Delivery fell from 22 minutes to 8.">
<span class="uc-face">
<span class="uc-pill">Pantry</span>
<strong>Delivery fell from 22 minutes to <b>8</b>.</strong>
<span class="uc-copy">Phone orders became a QR scan, and a late order now escalates on its own.</span>
<span class="uc-stats">
<span><b>8 min</b> average delivery, down from 22 minutes</span>
<span><b>97%</b> of orders on time, up from 68%</span>
<span><b>300+</b> pantry calls a day, now almost none</span>
<span><b>3</b> escalations a month, down from 40</span>
</span>
</span>
</a>
<a class="uc-card" href="/stories/facility-operations" aria-label="Energy. Energy cost is down 12%. After-hours power is billed to the tenant.">
<span class="uc-face">
<span class="uc-pill">Energy</span>
<strong>Energy cost is down <b>12%</b>. After-hours power is billed to the tenant.</strong>
<span class="uc-copy">Meter readings left paper and now run at set times through the day.</span>
<span class="uc-stats">
<span><b>12%</b> lower energy bills once spikes were fixed</span>
<span><b>9 pm</b> cutoff, so after-hours use is measured</span>
<span><b>100%</b> of meter readings were on paper before</span>
<span><b>0%</b> of after-hours tenant power was billed before</span>
</span>
</span>
</a>
<a class="uc-card" href="/stories/facility-operations" aria-label="Checklists. Compliance rose from 61% to 95%.">
<span class="uc-face">
<span class="uc-pill">Checklists</span>
<strong>Compliance rose from 61% to <b>95%</b>.</strong>
<span class="uc-copy">Cleaning schedules differed by campus. The same digital checklist now closes with a photo.</span>
<span class="uc-stats">
<span><b>95%</b> checklist compliance, up from 61%</span>
<span><b>96%</b> of PPM tasks done on time, up from 52%</span>
<span><b>45%</b> fewer unplanned breakdowns</span>
<span><b>14</b> campuses on one cleaning schedule</span>
</span>
</span>
</a>
<a class="uc-card" href="/stories/pantry" aria-label="Orders. 300+ phone orders a day became a QR scan.">
<span class="uc-face">
<span class="uc-pill">Orders</span>
<strong><b>300+</b> phone orders a day became a QR scan.</strong>
<span class="uc-copy">Calls were missed or written down wrong. People now order from the room they are in.</span>
<span class="uc-stats">
<span><b>300+</b> phone orders a day, now almost none</span>
<span><b>30 sec</b> to place an order, with no app</span>
<span><b>0%</b> of orders had a written record before</span>
<span><b>18</b> meeting rooms, each with its own menu</span>
</span>
</span>
</a>
<a class="uc-card" href="/stories/asset-management" aria-label="Register. 1,860 assets on site were missing from the books.">
<span class="uc-face">
<span class="uc-pill">Register</span>
<strong><b>1,860</b> assets on site were missing from the books.</strong>
<span class="uc-copy">Finance only knew what had been invoiced. The audit put the assets that exist onto one register.</span>
<span class="uc-stats">
<span><b>1,860</b> assets found with no record</span>
<span><b>4,120</b> ghost assets taken off the books</span>
<span><b>37</b> assets tied to more than one invoice</span>
<span><b>8 wks</b> to a clean digital register</span>
</span>
</span>
</a>
<a class="uc-card" href="/stories/facility-operations" aria-label="Visibility. 32,000+ assets, visible from one place.">
<span class="uc-face">
<span class="uc-pill">Visibility</span>
<strong><b>32,000+</b> assets, visible from one place.</strong>
<span class="uc-copy">Breakdowns used to stay on the campus. The central team now sees every site, asset, and open task.</span>
<span class="uc-stats">
<span><b>32,000+</b> assets on one system</span>
<span><b>1 in 3</b> breakdowns was reported before</span>
<span><b>45%</b> fewer unplanned breakdowns</span>
<span><b>14</b> campuses on one dashboard</span>
</span>
</span>
</a>
</div>
